d_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"text/plain; charset=utf-8","state":"uploaded","size":1839,"digest":"sha256:38c37c327e28b1da9f116ad34d52f4917f0bc14638b7d57a0801d61064874921","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-16T16:24:26Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T16:24:26Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m122-v0.12.2/M12STAGE2-SHA256SUMS.txt"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/assets/755553653","id":755553653,"node_id":"RA_kwDOVj6ISs4tCNV1","name":"m12stage2-starter-manifest.json","label":"","uploader":{"login":"enginsoysal","id":103884748,"node_id":"U_kgDOBjEnzA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103884748?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal","html_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/enginsoysal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":652,"digest":"sha256:d63f1e60aed7c15a8c92b2c321f21e6dc42d3a1508449b9905a83d1a9632a991","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-16T16:24:27Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T16:24:27Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m122-v0.12.2/m12stage2-starter-manifest.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/tarball/m122-v0.12.2","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/zipball/m122-v0.12.2","body":"# Engacer OS M12.2 / 0.12.2 — original scalable icons\n\nNative qualification passes **M12-STAGE2-VM-v1** on 16 November 2026.\n[Exact-source acceptance](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/c9cbec19fa3e2ed4da9eabba814d8927337e3edf/evidence/M12/2/acceptance-results.json) verifies\n573 compiled inputs, fourteen build/ZIP digests, 114 native app-icon comparisons,\ntwelve file/USB comparisons and twelve cached/full movement comparisons.\nPublic release and fresh website/download readback are separate required gates.\n\nBuild: `704df6a9802e5ba98e2062fec7922f57`.\nISO SHA256: `b95cd6cd2bb3e8aca6b2f85104f8b3af28484c2cc447d3a5f1f7b54f33111f64`.\nVMware ZIP SHA256: `aac14e766679fdcaa8702d55f4f8e064421e67917a28b6592ebc54e217836e08`.\n\n## What changes\n\nStart replaces letter badges with original recognizable app icons. Application\nidentities also appear on the taskbar and title bars. Folders, supported file\ntypes, shortcut overlays, USB rows, device categories and shared actions use the\nsame original geometric library. Names and established selection/activation\nbehavior remain. Broader desktop, Files/USB and taskbar layout work follows in\nthe ordered M12 stages.\n\nThe 57 icons share **2,443 bytes** of read-only geometry/colors, one **512-byte\ntemporary row** and **zero raster-cache bytes**. Fixed desktop BSS/data remains\n544,164 bytes; separate icon telemetry occupies a 32-byte storage span. Tested\nicon previews retain no additional managed pages or app processes. Existing\nfont coverage remains 251,248 bytes. These are distinct measurements, not total\nkernel consumption. [Resources](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/c9cbec19fa3e2ed4da9eabba814d8927337e3edf/evidence/M12/2/resources.json) and\n[implementation decisions](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/c9cbec19fa3e2ed4da9eabba814d8927337e3edf/docs/architecture/icons-m122.md) give exact scope.\n\n## Install and try\n\n[Follow the eight-step VMware guide](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/c9cbec19fa3e2ed4da9eabba814d8927337e3edf/docs/handbook/install-m122.md), then\n[recognize apps and files](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/c9cbec19fa3e2ed4da9eabba814d8927337e3edf/docs/handbook/icons-m122.md).\nUse `EngacerOS-M12STAGE2-VMware.zip` or its matching\n`EngacerOS-M12STAGE2.iso`. The ZIP contains a new blank growable 20-GiB SATA disk,\n128 MiB configured RAM, two CPUs and UEFI with Secure Boot off. All shipped\ndevices remain enabled. The matching ISO may remain connected after installation.\n\nThe twenty release assets include media, native images/maps, build/starter\nmanifests, notices, corresponding 7-Zip source and license material.\n`M12STAGE2-SHA256SUMS.txt` covers the other nineteen files.\n[Official release](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/tag/m122-v0.12.2).\n\n## What was checked and what remains\n\nThe exact enabled-device VMware ZIP installs and reaches its real installed\ndesktop, then boots twice without its ISO using the same firmware variables.\nQEMU SATA/UEFI and BIOS have separate installation/retained-ISO/two-disk-boot\njourneys. Actual 100/150/200% app-icon pixels match the host rasterizer in both\nthemes, including a real 3840×2160 framebuffer. Native file types, unknown\nfallback, real FAT32 USB rows, safe removal, provider focus, scrolling, idle and\nsigned cached/full window movement pass. Independent file CRCs confirm that the\nsample contents remain intact. Icon appearance does not qualify another file\ndecoder, GPU acceleration or Windows application runtime.\n\n**Retained unresolved observation:** an earlier M12.2 candidate had an initial\nconcurrent BIOS installation hit the existing AHCI timeout and report failure;\na fresh repeat of that candidate passed its complete journey. The corrected\npalette candidate has its own matching results. The trigger is not isolated. The failed report is\npreserved under diagnostics. This stage does not qualify stress reliability;\nfinal qualification must revisit this rather than treating the repeat as a fix.\n\nThe full controller/device/original-app regression remains **M12.18**. Physical\nhardware, ARM, vendor GPU 3D, universal DOS/Windows compatibility and a human\nusability study are not qualified. The homepage feature is an actual owned QEMU\ninstalled-guest capture, distinct from the host artwork contact sheets.\n"}